#basePath P3_TroutPop_Action
#include "Header.leaf"

:: Start
@exposed
@cutscene

// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P3_TroutPop_Action"

//Changes dialogue depending on whether stock cisco is already done
$if global:stockCisco == true
       {@}
              Neveah is still looking over the pools. 

       {@Neveah}
              Come back for more? A nice picnic with the fishies?

       {@You}
              Sorry, no fish picnic at the moment, but I need your help with something else.

       {@Neveah}
              What's up?

       {@You}
              You know how you told me cisco can be added back into the lake. I was wondering if that would also be possible with trout?

       {Neveah}
              Ooo, yes. We can definitely add them to the lake, if you'd like. 
       $call GiveActionCard("Action-stock-lake-trout")

       {@You}
              That would be amazing. Thanks for your help. 

       {@Neveah}
              Of course, friend!
              Oh, and about that free portrait that I told you about earlier...

       {@}
              She hands you a small canvas, barely larger than your palm. It's a sea lamprey. 

       {@Neveah}
              You said you didn't have any pets. So, I figured this was the next best thing. 

       {@}
              You think about the torn photo in your pocket, but it's less heavy.

       {@You}
              This is beautiful, Neveah. Thank you. Really.

       {@}
              She pulls you into a tight hug. 
              Back in your car, you put the photo on the dash, and the sea lamprey almost seems to smile at you. 
$elseif global:stockCisco == false
       {@}
              The hatchery is... different than what you imagined. 
              Rows of deep pools remind you of your university's pool. But with the mass of athletes replaced with tightly-packed scales.
              At the edge of one of the rows, an aquaculture specialist looks lovingly into the water.

       {@Specialist}
              Hello, George. Hello, Henrietta. Hello, Sir Troutsalot. 

       {@You}
              Um, hello?

       {@Specialist}
              Ooo, hi there. I'm Neveah!

       {@You}
              Ana. I've actually come to talk to you about the trout.

       {@Neveah}
              I'd love to talk about my fish children. That's what I call them. The trout.

       {@You}
              Makes sense. Have you ever released these fish into the wild?

       {@Neveah}
              Ooo, yes, we've done that before! It's been helpful to the population in the lake in the past.

       {@You}   
              Well, that's good news. Do you think that would be possible to do now?
              
       {@Neveah}
              Oh, definitely. I'm sure you'll take excellent care of my fishies.
       $call GiveActionCard("Action-stock-lake-trout")

       {@You}
              I'll definitely do my best. 

       {@Neveah}
              Yay! That's a plan, then. Oooo, I'm very excited. Do you have any fish?

       {@You}
              Uhhh, no. 

       {@Neveah}
              Aw, man. I do fish portraiture. Very glamorous. I'd like to give you a portrait, but if you don't have a pet...
              I'll figure something out!

       {@You}
              Oh, no, no, you really don't have to.

       {@Neveah}
              Nope, too late! Okay, bye bye now. I've got trout to look after!

       {@}
              Before you have time to say anything, she's back to greeting the fish. 

       $set global:stockTrout = true
$endif

// skip to end
$goto .End


:: End
@exposed
@tracked

// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P3_Hub.Continue